 spectral_norm's mixed operands)."] [234 1 "// tpName is a type's tp_name: a built-in type of another module than builtins named with it."] [242 1 "// seqConcatError is PyNumber_Add's sequence fallback when neither operand adds: str's, list's and tuple's sq_concat"] [243 1 "// and the bytes-like buffers' refuse b in their own words (nil for any other a)."] [262 1 "// overridesReflected is b's type a proper subtype of a's whose reflected method is its own."] [298 1 "// InPlaceOp is a op= b: the in-place method, else BinaryOp."] [301 17 "// int and float have no in-place methods"] [324 1 "// UnaryOp is +o, -o or ~o."] [335 1 "// RichCompare is a op b (PyObject_RichCompare: the C level's recursion check, then do_richcompare)."] [337 2 "// two exact ints or two exact floats: their own comparison, which recurses into nothing (202b)"] [357 1 "// doRichCompare is do_richcompare: a's method, then b's swapped one, then identity for == and !=."] [387 1 "// Eq is a == b as a Go bool (identity first, as PyObject_RichCompareBool)."] [399 1 "// GetAttr is getattr(o, name)."] [414 1 "// Call is f(*args) with the last len(kwnames) of args keyword arguments."] [423 1 "// GetIter is iter(o)."] [434 1 "// Next is next(it): (nil, nil) at the end."] [443 1 "// GetItem is o[key]."] [445 2 "// an exact list's or tuple's item at an int in range: the slot's answer without its conversions (202b)"] [476 1 "// seqIter is the iterator of a type with __getitem__ and no __iter__ (PY5b: its type registered)."] [515 1 "// isSeqRepeat is a type with sq_repeat."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[36 22] [67 22] [90 27] [97 27] [147 39] [154 36] [182 49] [193 39] [199 49] [300 39] [303 36] [313 36] [326 34] [340 23] [344 25] [360 30] [366 36] [372 36] [403 32] [425 29] [446 24] [454 28] [464 32] [467 23] [468 41] [502 29]]} (go/file "abstract.go" :imports [

